 # Particle System Renderer
 
-
 ## Overview
-The Particle System Renderer (PSR) is a general-purpose, object-order rendering system that converts discrete, time-evolving particles into rasterized images by managing explicit particle lifecycles and projecting them onto a defined viewport [S1, unofficial]. It solves the visualization problem for Radar Cross Section (RCS) data and other discrete distributions by procedurally generating particles from centroids and accumulating their contributions via a CPU-based linked-list architecture [S1, unofficial]. Unlike [Billboards and particles](9045-billboards-and-particles.md) which rely on fixed 2D quads, or [Screen-Space Fluid Rendering Pipeline](14414-screen-space-fluid-rendering-pipeline.md) which uses GPU-accelerated screen-space techniques, PSR explicitly tracks spawn/die states and supports procedural centroid-based generation on the CPU [S1, unofficial][G].
+The Particle System Renderer (PSR) is a general-purpose, object-order rendering system that converts discrete, time-evolving particles into rasterized images by managing explicit particle lifecycles and projecting them onto a defined viewport [S1, unofficial]. It solves the visualization problem for Radar Cross Section (RCS) data and other discrete distributions by procedurally generating particles from centroids and accumulating their contributions via a CPU-based linked-list architecture [S1, unofficial]. Unlike [Billboards and particles](9045-billboards-and-particles.md), which rely on fixed 2D quads, or [Screen-Space Fluid Rendering Pipeline](14414-screen-space-fluid-rendering-pipeline.md), which uses GPU-accelerated screen-space techniques, PSR explicitly tracks spawn/die states and supports procedural centroid-based generation on the CPU [S1, unofficial][G].
 
